  "title": "Authentication Overview",
  "description": "Understand authentication and why it's important.",
  "order": 1,
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedMinutes": 18,
  "tags": ["authentication", "security", "overview", "basics"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Authentication** is the process of verifying who a user is. **Authorization** determines what an authenticated user can access."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Why Authentication Matters"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Protect sensitive data**: Only authorized users access data",
          "**Personalization**: Show user-specific content",
          "**Audit trails**: Track who did what",
          "**Compliance**: Meet security regulations"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Common Methods"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**Password-based**: Username and password",
          "**Multi-factor**: Password + SMS/authenticator",
          "**Social login**: Google, Facebook, GitHub",
          "**Biometric**: Fingerprint, face recognition"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "info",
        "title": "Never Store Plain Passwords",
        "text": "Always hash passwords using bcrypt, Argon2, or PBKDF2. Never store passwords in plain text."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
          "Authentication verifies identity",
          "Authorization controls access",
          "Multiple authentication methods",
          "Never store plain passwords"
        ],
        "takeaway": "Authentication is fundamental to application security."
      }
    }
  ],
